# Generated, committed artifacts whose form carries WHOLE-FILE state — content
# hashes and tallies — and which are therefore REGENERATED, never merged
# (issue #3069).
#
# The `regenerated` driver runs the ordinary 3-way merge first and keeps a clean
# result; only on a genuine conflict does it take ours and mark the path, and
# `scripts/resolve-generated-artifacts.ts` re-derives it once at the rebased tip.
#
# The driver itself lives in LOCAL git config (it cannot be committed) and is
# registered by `bun run worktree:init`. Without that registration git falls
# back to the default text merge, i.e. exactly the behaviour that predates this
# file — a missing bootstrap degrades, it does not corrupt.
#
# This list is not hand-maintained: `scripts/__tests__/generated-artifact-merge.test.ts`
# pins it to REGENERATED_ARTIFACTS in `scripts/lib/generated-artifacts.ts`,
# which also records why every OTHER committed `data/` artifact is out of the
# class.
data/oracle-compiled.json merge=regenerated
data/oracle-legality.json merge=regenerated
